    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d673">

                <pb facs="0702" n="690" sameAs="frus:frus1941v01/pg690"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.61/786: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Steinhardt</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-01-20T20:00:00+03:00">January 20, 1941—8
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 10:20 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>116. In the course of a conversation Saturday night<anchor n="76"
                        xml:id="d673-f1"/> with Mikoyan,<anchor n="77" xml:id="d673-f2"/> he
                    expressed his disappointment in a good-natured manner with the failure of the
                    conversations in Washington to make further progress than they had, citing as an
                    example that “only 42% of the machine tools purchased and paid for by the Soviet
                    Union in the United States had thus far been released.”</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Steinhardt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d673-f1" n="76" xml:id="d673-f1-content">
